<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link><description>World News Today: Read the latest world news headlines, Current International breaking news world wide. In depth analysis and top news headlines world wide.</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-09-09T21:22:42+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/296589292.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Wed, 09 Sep 2026 21:22:42 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>World News, Today World News, Latest International News, World Breaking News, Trending News of World - Times of India</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Highway 141 takes Missouri family’s 15 acres; how $238,000 offer became $2.1 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133968882.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A Missouri family's 15-acre property, bought in 1904, became the centre of a long eminent domain dispute after St. Louis County acquired it for a highway project. A jury valued the land at $1.3 million, while the court added $650,000 in heritage value and interest, taking the judgment to about $2.1 million. The Missouri Supreme Court later upheld the award.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1904-a-missouri-family-acquired-15-acres-106-years-later-st-louis-county-condemned-it-for-highway-141-and-a-238000-offer-became-a-2-1-million-judgment-upheld-on-appeal/articleshow/133968882.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/in-1904-a-missouri-family-acquired-15-acres-106-years-later-st-louis-county-condemned-it-for-highway-141-and-a-238000-offer-became-a-2-1-million-judgment-upheld-on-appeal/articleshow/133968882.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T20:57:40+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133970516,imgsize-148972.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Couple bought a broken Eichler home; now it’s worth $2.75 million]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133973166.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A magnificent example of midcentury modern architecture, this rare 1971 Eichler home in San Anselmo is listed at $2.75 million. Boasting four bedrooms, it has been tastefully renovated since its acquisition in 2015, showcasing an inviting indoor-outdoor aesthetic, a contemporary kitchen, and a sparkling pool. This home blends vibrant living spaces, making it perfect for families and older adults seeking style and comfort.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2015-a-california-couple-bought-a-distressed-1971-eichler-home-at-auction-11-years-later-their-fully-restored-house-one-of-just-15-eichlers-in-the-area-is-asking-2-75m/articleshow/133973166.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/real-estate/news/in-2015-a-california-couple-bought-a-distressed-1971-eichler-home-at-auction-11-years-later-their-fully-restored-house-one-of-just-15-eichlers-in-the-area-is-asking-2-75m/articleshow/133973166.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-09-09T20:12:24+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Real Estate Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https